  "notes": "Modified cash basis city; only a General Fund (governmental) and Combined Utilities Fund (business-type). Governmental figures from p4 statement (General Fund is the only governmental fund, so no total column). Beginning cash = beginning fund balance 758,696 (cash basis, p4); ending cash 1,035,050 = cash 478,595 + CDs 542,644 + county treasurer 13,811 (p3). Governmental roll-forward ties: 758,696 + 1,473,726 - 1,308,872 + 111,500 = 1,035,050. Business-type roll-forward uses net position (562,345 to 792,918; cash would be 849,558) and ties: +2,519,897 - 2,177,824 - 111,500 transfers out. Business-type receipts: operating revenues only (no nonoperating revenues). Operating expense lines classed utilities except Capital outlay. Government-wide Total column used for balance sheet (p1); component unit (Rescue Squad) excluded. The p9 budget-basis All Funds schedule (state receipts 563,303, other local receipts 3,012,556 etc.) mixes governmental and utility funds with broad groups and was not entered in detail; statements p4/p6 are more detailed. LB840 is a component of the General Fund; its lines are in detail only (sales tax 94,943 is within the General Fund sales tax on p4 presumably). Governmental 'Intergovernmental' 535,380 = unrestricted state revenues 494,613 + public safety grants 40,767 per p2, kept as printed. p8 (proprietary cash flow reconciliation, added by the v8 re-trim) confirms net cash from operating activities 880,323; nothing new to record. Read pages 1-10 of 10",
